-- gap[104] · a DERIVED constant — the condition names nothing the reader can
-- see is 42, and the compiler still proves it.
--
-- `a + b` has to be folded before `c > 10` is decidable, so this row fails if
-- the fold reaches one level and not two. It is the smallest fixture here that
-- an author could not have written as a literal, which is the point: the blast
-- radius is "conditions the optimizer proves", not "conditions spelled with a
-- literal", and those are not the same set.

main = (): i64
    a = 20
    b = 22
    c = a + b
    if c > 10
        print("derived")
        print("derivedlast")
    print("after")
    0
